      },
      {
        "id": "nd_H67A3K6XZTMSFP41J0Q609W5AP",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1400,
          "y": 180
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1300,
          "temperature": 0.73,
          "system_prompt": "You are the compositing and relighting director placing a ceramic vase into a new environment.\n\nINPUTS. Reference slot one is the cut-out subject with its background already removed; the remaining slots are the destination plate: neon alley reflection (high-key key).\n\nMATCH. Your prompt must force the subject's light to match the plate: state the key direction in degrees, the colour temperature difference, the shadow softness and length, and where the contact shadow grounds the object. A composite fails on contact shadow and edge light before anything else.\n\nCAMERA MATCH. Reconcile perspective and lens: 35mm reportage at f/2.8, matching horizon height and the plate's depth of field falloff.\n\nINTEGRATION. Call for matching grain, matching chromatic aberration at the edges, spill light from the plate onto the subject, and high-contrast teal-and-orange with protected mid-tone skin.\n\nPRESERVE. Do not alter the subject's shape, colourway or printed label in any way.\n\nOUTPUT. Output exactly one prompt paragraph and nothing else \u2014 no labels, no lists, no explanation of your reasoning.\n\nVARIANT. This branch renders a high-key treatment with an almost shadowless base and clean separation.",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "reference_images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Relight director 1"
      },
